{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-crankcase-running fixture",
    "description": "The `process-crankcase-running` fixture: the run's EXECUTION database -- the snapshot's own tables, cut from the default database for this RunSpec and holding its generators' intermediate tables -- mounted on `onroad/model.esm`. It holds no logic: its `data_sources` are the catalogue under the names the model reads, and its one model, `Fixture`, mounts the domain model as a SUBSYSTEM, binds the run's declared counts, and carries the run's inline tests: assertions on the mounted model's intermediate values (`Onroad.*` / `Nonroad.*`) against this snapshot. A test written inside a `{ref}`'d model does not run (finding F47), so the assertions live here, in the document that supplies the data they are about (esm-spec §6.6; conventions §106). run-tests.sh's fixture stage runs them, then emits the model's `out_*` relation and compares it with the snapshot's MOVESOutput. `runspecs/process-crankcase-running.esm` reproduces the same run from the DEFAULT database through the same model, so the pair is a differential test of the execution-database cut: one model, one oracle, two catalogues.\n\nUntil 2026-10-30 this file inlined its own copy of the onroad model (19390 lines, frozen at the commit that last touched it), so the logic every fixture shared was written fourteen times. PLAN.md §7.1, docs/esm-conventions.md §106."
  },
  "models": {
    "Fixture": {
      "subsystems": {
        "Onroad": {
          "ref": "catalogues/onroad-execution-db.esm",
          "url_substitutions": {
            "snapshot": "process-crankcase-running"
          },
          "bindings": {
            "n_outputRate": 684
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {},
      "equations": [],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_run_scope_comes_from_the_execution_database",
          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610 -- byte for byte `process-tirewear`'s and `process-brakewear`'s scope, so the whole activity half of this fixture is already checked end to end by two others. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7 and it is the authority (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1). The columns after the temperature and heat index are new here: the two humidity columns the NOx correction reads, and the GPA fraction that selects the fuel effects' ordinary arm.\n\nTHE TWO HUMIDITY ROWS FACE THE REFERENCE ACROSS THIS DOCUMENT'S OWN ARITHMETIC (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4). Their `expected` is what `ZoneMonthHour` STORES; since docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 the value under test is not that column but MG-4 to MG-7 run here from `temperature`, `relHumidity` and `County.barometricPressure`. Measured, the port lands 10.053684062398 against the stored 10.053684293477 (2.2985e-08 relative) and 0.015929058669 against 0.015929059029 (2.2619e-08). Those two rows therefore carry `rel: 1e-7` -- four times the worse of the pair, the gate components/meteorology.esm asserts the whole generator at, and 200x tighter than tolerance.toml's per-cell 2e-05. Every other row here is a key and stays exact.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_yearID",
              "time": 0.0,
