        {
          "id": "the_six_pollutant_processes_are_three_pollutants_on_two_processes",
          "description": "The run's whole scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. THIS IS THE FIRST FIXTURE IN THE PORT WITH TWO PROCESSES ON THE SAME POLLUTANTS: 101/201/301 are Running Exhaust and come off the `BaseRateCalculator` spine; 115/215/315 are Crankcase Running Exhaust and are chained off their own pollutant's exhaust row by `CrankcaseEmissionCalculatorNonPM`. The chain declaration is MOVES's, read from `runspecchainedto`; this test pins the six (pollutant, process) pairs, and not the chain inputs, whose per-row variable is gone (the chain is now the `lnk_*` edge list).",
