        {
          "id": "125_cohorts_are_selected_124_are_rated_and_104_carry_a_crankcase_ratio",
          "description": "THE STRUCTURAL CLAIM OF THIS RUNG, and no row count can make it. S10 selects 125 of the 164 candidates for each of the three EXHAUST pollutant-processes and none at all for the three crankcase ones -- `pollutantprocessmodelyear` carries no 115/215/315 row, so a crankcase pollutant-process is not a rate path in this document any more than it is in MOVES. Of the 125, ONE is unrated: electricity model year 2000 (rate row 144) is selected and `emissionratebyage` has no row for it, so 124 exhaust rows emit. Of those 124, 104 carry a crankcase ratio -- the twenty electricity cohorts do not, because `crankcaseemissionratio` has no fuelTypeID 9 row and MOVES's join is an inner one. 3 x 124 + 3 x 104 = 684 emitting rate rows, and 684 x 2 day types is the 1368 the snapshot has.\n\nWHAT IS ASSERTED is the one unrated row: rate row 144 is electricity model year 2000, selected, not surviving and not emitting. The per-pollutant-process selected and emitted counts, the 684 total and the output ranks that asserted the rest are gone from the model, and `cohortSurvivorCount` now counts the cohorts the output carries (124, not 125); none of those is asserted here.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
